      en: "Mount Fentale is an active stratovolcano in the Afar Region of Ethiopia, rising to 1,017 m. Its caldera is about 2 km in diameter and contains a crater lake. The last eruption was in 1825. The volcano is composed primarily of basaltic lava flows. The surrounding landscape is arid, with sparse vegetation. Fentale is located within the Awash National Park and is a popular hiking destination. The volcano is part of the East African Rift system. Geothermal activity is evident through hot springs.",
